## ## 3. All Common Fields & What They Do

| Field | Purpose | Scenario |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`container_name`** | Overrides Docker's default naming. | Use this for your TikTok demos so the names look clean. |
| **`environment`** | Passes passwords, API keys, or settings. | Essential for Databases or WordPress. |
| **`depends_on`** | Tells Docker "Don't start App A until Database B is ready." | Use this when building multi-container apps. |
| **`working_dir`** | Sets the "Starting Folder" inside the container. | Great for custom scripts. |
| **`command`** | Overrides the default command in the Dockerfile. | Use this to run `ls -la` or specific scripts on start. |
| **`build`** | Instead of an `image`, it points to a local `Dockerfile`. | Use this when you are building your own apps from scratch. |

